WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
A lab culture of Paramecium cells.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.510
They multiply fast.

3
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.430
Then the growth levels off, at about
300 cells per cubic centimetre.

4
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.950
Now the human line.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.460
2.49 billion people in 1950.

6
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:18.090
8.16 billion in 2024.

7
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:22.730
Our growth rate peaked in
1963, and is far lower today.

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.910
So is there a ceiling for us too?

9
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.090
How many people can one planet,
or one country, really support?

10
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.630
In this mission, you'll test
the ideas of overpopulation,

11
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.670
underpopulation and optimum population.

12
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.510
Then you'll trace the
feedback loops linking people,

13
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.150
food, resources and pollution.

14
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.690
Your mission: work out what limits
the number of people a planet,

15
00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.880
or a country, can support.
